#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# region_measure

#% text
# `region_measure(reg)` is the measure of the region in its own dimension: the length of a curve, the area of a surface, the volume of a solid; 0 for points.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact coordinates give exact results; symbolic ones give formulas.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A disk and a ball of radius r:

#% cell
[region_measure(disk([0, 0], r)), region_measure(ball([0, 0, 0], r))]
#% output
#= [pi*r^2, (4/3)*pi*r^3]

#% text
# A polyline:

#% cell
region_measure(line([[0, 0], [1, 1], [1, 0]]))
#% output
#= 1 + 2^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# An ellipse's area:

#% cell
region_measure(disk([0, 0], [2, 3]))
#% output
#= 6*pi

#% text
# A rectangle with symbolic corners:

#% cell
region_measure(rectangle([a, b], [c, d]))
#% output
#= (c - a)*(d - b)

#% text
# A circle's length and a sphere's area:

#% cell
[region_measure(circle()), region_measure(sphere())]
#% output
#= [2*pi, 4*pi]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `area`, `volume`, `arc_length`, `region_centroid`
